{"seq":16,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/hermes-opus-no-style-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T11:16:52.075Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c40ac572032c786b0e80e6408e31d312b9c1feef55579ecbbea93880400749b6","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files: four North digests and two Central ones. I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. #PD-4492 is in \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14-18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments at gatehouse kiosk check-in. Support patched the SMS gateway routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift got through fine. The note also has an action item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. #4419 is in \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe other two North digests (9/14/2025 pipeline and 3/23/2026 renewals) mention QFL but don't give a ticket number. The Central digests have #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but none of them are QFL tickets. #4409 and #4412 are on a Central dealer account that Moss's handoff note ties to Marrow Fieldworks, and FR-882 belongs to Marrow Agrisupply. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company, a competitor's customer, so I left it out too.\n\nThe cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell whether #4419 is still open.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/hermes-opus-no-style-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T11:17:00.301Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"b9ab06198368ec819e61750f367603ee40068f7e6c3a3dc46856b0b77c2d6040","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I've sent Dana the list in our DM thread. Moss's notes give two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments when they checked in at the gatehouse kiosk. Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift checked in with no manual help.\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). The gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. Thea logged it, and it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell whether it's still open.\n\nI went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files, and these are the only two. The other two North digests mention Quarrendon Freight Lines but don't give a ticket number. The Central digests list #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are on other accounts. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a Pemberline customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
